From: rtw89-usb-ap-fix <local@patch>
Date: Sun, 7 Sep 2026 15:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] rtw89: skip HS probe for RTL8922A, wait for SuperSpeed

RTL8922AU on Raspberry Pi 4 (VL805 xHCI + VIA hub) enumerates at
high-speed first through the hub's USB2 path. rtw89_usb_switch_mode_be()
then reads PAD_CTRL2 and finds MATCH_CNT already equal to
USB_SWITCH_DELAY - the chip's power-on default - so it believes a USB3
switch was already attempted and returns 0. The driver proceeds with a
full probe over USB2, where every vendor request fails with -71.

After the probe fails the usb core disconnects the device, the dongle
resets back to its DISK (0bda:1a2b) mode, re-switches, and the whole
cycle repeats. On iStoreOS this burns ~90 seconds per boot, during
which the USB error storm knocks the on-board bcmgenet GbE link down
(WAN DHCP fails and the dongle has to be unplugged to boot cleanly),
and netifd gives up on the wifi radio before the phy ever registers.

Skip the full probe for RTL8922A whenever the device has not reached
SuperSpeed and USB3 switching is enabled. The usb core keeps the port
open and the device re-enumerates at SuperSpeed moments later, where
the normal probe succeeds. On a physical USB2-only port the device
simply stays unbound instead of error-storming.

Users who explicitly disable USB3 switching with switch_usb_mode=N
keep the old behavior and still get the HS probe.
---
diff --git a/usb.c b/usb.c
--- a/usb.c
+++ b/usb.c
@@ -1209,8 +1209,27 @@
 		ret = 0;
 		goto err_intf_deinit;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * RTL8922AU on RPi4: PAD_CTRL2 MATCH_CNT defaults to
+	 * USB_SWITCH_DELAY, so switch_mode_be() believes a USB3 switch
+	 * was already attempted and falls through to a full HS probe.
+	 * Vendor requests then fail with -71 and the device resets,
+	 * re-enumerates and repeats, taking ~90s per boot and knocking
+	 * the on-board GbE PHY offline in the meantime. Skip the HS
+	 * probe entirely and wait for SuperSpeed re-enumeration. On a
+	 * physical USB2 port the device simply stays unbound.
+	 */
+	if (rtwdev->chip->chip_id == RTL8922A &&
+	    rtwusb->udev->speed != USB_SPEED_SUPER &&
+	    rtw89_switch_usb_mode) {
+		rtw89_info(rtwdev,
+			   "skip HS probe for RTL8922A, wait for SuperSpeed re-enumeration\n");
+		ret = 0;
+		goto err_intf_deinit;
+	}
+
 	if (rtwusb->udev->speed == USB_SPEED_SUPER)
 		rtwdev->hci.dle_type = RTW89_HCI_DLE_TYPE_USB3;
 	else
 		rtwdev->hci.dle_type = RTW89_HCI_DLE_TYPE_USB2;
